WEBVTT

1
00:00:49.208 --> 00:00:53.291


2
00:00:53.291 --> 00:00:57.500
<b>Lord Krishna positioned the chariot</b>
<b>in the middle of the battlefield. </b>

3
00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:02.875
<b>it is exactly mentioned what Arjuna saw here. </b>

4
00:01:02.875 --> 00:01:06.291
<b>The son of Pritha, or the son of Kunti, Arjuna, </b>

5
00:01:06.291 --> 00:01:10.708
<b>saw in the armies present there</b>
<b>all his close relatives,</b>

6
00:01:10.708 --> 00:01:11.833
<b>paternal uncles,</b>

7
00:01:11.833 --> 00:01:12.833
<b>grandfathers,</b>

8
00:01:12.833 --> 00:01:13.666
<b>teachers,</b>

9
00:01:13.666 --> 00:01:14.666
<b>maternal uncles,</b>

10
00:01:14.666 --> 00:01:17.375
<b>all the sons and grandsons of the entire family, </b>

11
00:01:17.375 --> 00:01:18.291
<b>his fathers-in-law,</b>

12
00:01:18.291 --> 00:01:21.625
<b>and his friends and many people.</b>

13
00:01:21.625 --> 00:01:25.291
<b>The effect this had on Arjuna is also mentioned.</b>

14
00:01:25.291 --> 00:01:29.125
<b>the son of Kunti, Arjuna, was filled</b>
<b>with immense compassion...</b>

15
00:01:29.125 --> 00:01:34.000
<b>What Arjuna said after this is described</b>
<b>in the following verses.</b>

16
00:01:34.541 --> 00:01:38.791


17
00:01:38.791 --> 00:01:40.833
<b>This was indeed a battlefield,</b>

18
00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:43.708
<b>where there are either companions or enemies.</b>

19
00:01:43.708 --> 00:01:45.791
<b>Here too, there were two sides,</b>

20
00:01:45.791 --> 00:01:49.166
<b>one of the Kauravas and one of the Pandavas.</b>

21
00:01:49.166 --> 00:01:49.875
<b>But</b>

22
00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:56.041
<b>in this moment, Arjuna saw only his</b>
<b>loved ones in every direction.</b>

23
00:01:56.041 --> 00:02:01.291
<b>On one side were his grandfather</b>
<b>like personalities, Bhishma and Somadatta, </b>

24
00:02:01.291 --> 00:02:04.833
<b>and Bhurishrava, who was like a father.</b>

25
00:02:04.833 --> 00:02:06.291
<b>Arjuna's teachers,</b>

26
00:02:06.291 --> 00:02:07.416
<b>Dronacharya</b>

27
00:02:07.416 --> 00:02:10.125
<b>and Kripacharya, were also there, </b>

28
00:02:10.125 --> 00:02:13.250
<b>as were Shakuni and Shalya,</b>
<b>who were like uncles.</b>

29
00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:16.041
<b>On one side were his Pandava brothers, </b>

30
00:02:16.041 --> 00:02:19.541
<b>but on the other side stood the 100 Kauravas, </b>

31
00:02:19.541 --> 00:02:22.291
<b>who were also brothers. </b>

32
00:02:22.291 --> 00:02:23.791
<b>His son Abhimanyu was there, </b>

33
00:02:23.791 --> 00:02:30.166
<b>as well as young warriors who were</b>
<b>the age of Arjuna's grandsons. </b>

34
00:02:30.166 --> 00:02:34.208
<b>Ashwatthama and Jayadratha</b>
<b>were warriors of his own generation. </b>

35
00:02:34.208 --> 00:02:41.541
<b>His father-in-law King Drupada, and well-wishers</b>
<b>like Kritavarma and Bhagadatta, were all there.</b>

36
00:02:41.541 --> 00:02:43.541
<b>Seeing all these loved ones,</b>

37
00:02:43.541 --> 00:02:47.375
<b>a surge of emotion began to rise within Arjuna. </b>

38
00:02:47.375 --> 00:02:49.041
<b>His mind was agitated, </b>

39
00:02:49.041 --> 00:02:52.000
<b>thinking that due to the war,</b>
<b>in just a few moments, </b>

40
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.750
<b>would all these people be ready to</b>
<b>defeat each other, </b>

41
00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:58.541
<b>or even send each other to the jaws of death?</b>

42
00:02:58.541 --> 00:03:03.333
<b>Such thoughts had filled Arjuna</b>
<b>with compassion and sorrow.</b>

43
00:03:03.333 --> 00:03:09.041
<b>For a warrior on the battlefield to be</b>
<b>so overwhelmedwith emotion was unexpected.</b>

44
00:03:09.041 --> 00:03:13.458
<b>Even Arjuna himself had not thought</b>
<b>that he would become so emotional. </b>

45
00:03:13.458 --> 00:03:21.458
<b>After all, preparations for this war, to be fought </b>
<b>for their rights, had been going on for many years.</b>

46
00:03:21.458 --> 00:03:24.208
<b>So why today? Why like this?</b>

47
00:03:24.833 --> 00:03:28.958


48
00:03:28.958 --> 00:03:33.166
<b>A human being will be reduced</b>
<b>to a mere machine</b>

49
00:03:33.166 --> 00:03:38.916
<b>if emotions are completely lost.</b>
<b>Emotions are the very essence </b>

50
00:03:38.916 --> 00:03:43.958
<b>that adds flavor to life.</b>

51
00:03:43.958 --> 00:03:47.041
<b>Emotions are like the ingredients</b>

52
00:03:47.041 --> 00:03:50.166
<b>that make a delicious meal,</b>

53
00:03:50.166 --> 00:03:58.125
<b>like the colors with which an artist creates</b>
<b>a captivating painting.</b>

54
00:03:58.125 --> 00:03:59.666
<b>However,</b>

55
00:03:59.666 --> 00:04:04.000
<b>if too much salt falls into the food,</b>

56
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.833
<b>the taste will turn bitter;</b>

57
00:04:06.833 --> 00:04:13.000
<b>if a single color is smeared across a painting,</b>

58
00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:17.791
<b>it will no longer please the eyes.</b>

59
00:04:17.791 --> 00:04:20.125
<b>The right balance,</b>

60
00:04:20.125 --> 00:04:24.625
<b>the right balance is the rule of nature.</b>

61
00:04:24.625 --> 00:04:26.375
<b>In the same way,</b>

62
00:04:26.375 --> 00:04:27.875
<b>Good or bad,</b>

63
00:04:27.875 --> 00:04:30.958
<b>any excessive emotion, </b>

64
00:04:30.958 --> 00:04:33.416
<b>can be harmful.</b>

65
00:04:33.416 --> 00:04:39.458
<b>Someone may constantly try</b>
<b>to deceive or harm us,</b>

66
00:04:39.458 --> 00:04:44.000
<b>but because of our love, we may overlook it all.</b>

67
00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.666
<b>It's possible</b>

68
00:04:45.666 --> 00:04:51.541
<b>that due to bitterness, we may disregard</b>
<b>someone's good suggestions.</b>

69
00:04:51.541 --> 00:04:57.000
<b>Just as every color has its place in a rainbow, </b>

70
00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:00.458
<b>every note has its inherent position in a song, </b>

71
00:05:00.458 --> 00:05:02.750
<b>in the same way,</b>

72
00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:08.416
<b>logic and emotions have their</b>
<b>respective places in life.</b>

73
00:05:08.416 --> 00:05:13.541
<b>It is necessary to maintain balance.</b>

74
00:05:13.541 --> 00:05:15.000
<b>But</b>

75
00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:19.500
<b>life will also bring many situations</b>

76
00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:27.041
<b>where the wave of emotions will rise in such a</b>
<b>way that the boat of the mind will drift away.</b>

77
00:05:27.041 --> 00:05:29.666
<b>Despite being a great warrior,</b>

78
00:05:29.666 --> 00:05:34.666
<b>this is what is happening</b>
<b>to Arjuna at this moment.</b>

79
00:05:34.666 --> 00:05:36.958
<b>Now he is in my shelter, </b>

80
00:05:36.958 --> 00:05:38.333
<b>and so are you.</b>

81
00:05:38.333 --> 00:05:40.333
<b>Be at peace. </b>

82
00:05:40.333 --> 00:05:42.416
<b>The waves will subside,</b>

83
00:05:42.416 --> 00:05:44.625
<b>and the boat will also reach the shore.</b>

84
00:05:45.291 --> 00:05:49.416


85
00:05:49.416 --> 00:05:54.000
<b>In your life too, there will be situations</b>

86
00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:59.416
<b>where it will seem like you</b>
<b>and your family are in a conflict. </b>

87
00:05:59.416 --> 00:06:01.208
<b>You are on one side,</b>

88
00:06:01.208 --> 00:06:04.708
<b>and the family is on the other.</b>

89
00:06:04.708 --> 00:06:08.000
<b>What do you do in such a situation?</b>

90
00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.208
<b>Assuming that someone's feelings</b>
<b>might get hurt,</b>

91
00:06:11.208 --> 00:06:22.208
<b>do you go against your own mind,</b>
<b>even if you don't want to?</b>

92
00:06:22.208 --> 00:06:26.541
<b>But in such a situation,</b>

93
00:06:26.541 --> 00:06:31.583
<b>do you somewhere end up blaming others?</b>

94
00:06:31.583 --> 00:06:33.500
<b>Not with anger, </b>

95
00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:34.875
<b>not with bitterness, </b>

96
00:06:34.875 --> 00:06:38.333
<b>and not by getting carried away by emotions. </b>

97
00:06:38.333 --> 00:06:43.666
<b>In such situations, you will have to</b>
<b>work with harmony. </b>

98
00:06:43.666 --> 00:06:48.500
<b>Your family also wouldn't want bad for you, right?</b>

99
00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:49.750
<b>In such cases,</b>

100
00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:57.083
<b>the way out will be through reasoning and</b>
<b>introspection with the family and your inner self, </b>

101
00:06:57.083 --> 00:07:00.416
<b>not through the rush of emotions.</b>

102
00:07:00.416 --> 00:07:02.000
<b>Because</b>

103
00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:08.041
<b> if a decision is going to have a</b>
<b>profound impact on your life, </b>

104
00:07:08.041 --> 00:07:10.750
<b>then whatever the decision may be, </b>

105
00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:14.583
<b>you will have to take responsibility for it yourself.</b>

106
00:07:15.083 --> 00:07:19.041


107
00:07:19.041 --> 00:07:20.708
<b>Emotions </b>

108
00:07:20.708 --> 00:07:22.791
<b>are momentary, </b>

109
00:07:22.791 --> 00:07:24.125
<b>but </b>

110
00:07:24.125 --> 00:07:29.791
<b>the decisions taken under their influence are not. </b>

111
00:07:29.791 --> 00:07:34.625
<b>The impact of those decisions remains lifelong.</b>

112
00:07:34.625 --> 00:07:36.041
<b>Many times,</b>

113
00:07:36.041 --> 00:07:41.750
<b>we work for a very long time for an opportunity, </b>

114
00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:44.500
<b>and then suddenly </b>

115
00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:49.958
<b>that opportunity stands right in front of us. </b>

116
00:07:49.958 --> 00:07:58.458
<b>We get nervous because somewhere</b>
<b>we had only imagined that opportunity, </b>

117
00:07:58.458 --> 00:08:07.916
<b>but today when the time has come,</b>
<b>it seems like something might go wrong. </b>

118
00:08:07.916 --> 00:08:10.333
<b>Now that the opportunity is here, </b>

119
00:08:10.333 --> 00:08:18.875
<b>it comes to mind that to fulfill it,</b>
<b>we will have to pay a heavy price</b>

120
00:08:18.875 --> 00:08:25.500
<b>That price may be in terms of physical labor</b>
<b>or mental pressure.</b>

121
00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:29.500
<b>It's natural for such feelings to arise in the mind. </b>

122
00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:30.666
<b>But</b>

123
00:08:30.666 --> 00:08:36.833
<b>decisions cannot be made in the flow</b>
<b>of these emotions.</b>

124
00:08:36.833 --> 00:08:39.958
<b>There must be a deep reason </b>

125
00:08:39.958 --> 00:08:44.250
<b>why you were waiting for that opportunity</b>
<b>until now, right? </b>

126
00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:46.291
<b>Preparing for it?</b>

127
00:08:46.291 --> 00:08:50.500
<b>Then why be nervous now?</b>

128
00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:52.875
<b>Move forward with a calm mind. </b>

129
00:08:52.916 --> 00:08:57.500
<b>If this opportunity was not right for you,</b>

130
00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:01.583
<b>neither would you have</b>
<b>kept making efforts for it, </b>

131
00:09:01.583 --> 00:09:06.041
<b>nor would God have brought you to this stage. </b>

132
00:09:06.041 --> 00:09:07.625
<b>Have faith </b>

133
00:09:07.625 --> 00:09:10.166
<b>in yourself, </b>

134
00:09:10.166 --> 00:09:12.625
<b> and in God too. </b>

135
00:09:12.625 --> 00:09:15.750
<b>If you are walking with righteousness, </b>

136
00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:18.000
<b>everything will be auspicious.</b>

